hen the reward is claimed. Players will see them appear in their inventory but won't see them during the roll animation."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#custom-reward-types-with-hooks","content":"Use custom reward types to handle non-item rewards like vehicles or bank deposits. Register hooks in your own resource to handle these reward types."},"1183":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#lootbox-config-with-custom-rewards","content":"If a custom `rewardType` is set but no hook is registered, the system will log a warning and fall back to treating it as a regular item. This prevents rewards from being lost but may not give the intended reward."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#removing-a-hook","content":"You can remove a previously registered hook if needed:"},"1185":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"page","content":"Framework Setup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Free Resources","Lootbox"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup"},"1186":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-0","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works","content":"How It Works"},"1187":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-1","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#ox_core--ox_inventory-setup","content":"ox_core + ox_inventory Setup"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-2","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Item Definition Format"},"1189":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-3","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"How It Works (ox_core)"},"1190":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-4","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Complete Example"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-5","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Resource Order"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-6","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"QBCore / Qbox Setup"},"1193":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-7","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Item Definition Format"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-8","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"How It Works (QBCore / Qbox)"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-9","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Complete Example"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-10","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"Resource Order"},"1197":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-11","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#reference-file","content":"Reference File"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-12","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#adding-custom-lootboxes","content":"Adding Custom Lootboxes"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-13","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-14","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"Item does nothing when used"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-15","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#no-supported-framework-detected-warning","content":"\"No supported framework detected\" warning"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-16","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#lootbox-opens-but-no-item-is-given","content":"Lootbox opens but no item is given"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-17","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","content":"Each framework handles usable items differently. This page explains how to configure your item definitions so that lootbox cases work correctly with your framework and inventory system."},"1204":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-18","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","content":"These steps are **in addition** to defining your lootboxes in `config.lua`. You must also ensure the item definitions exist in your inventory/framework so players can hold and use the items."},"1205":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-19","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true` (the default), sleepless\\_lootbox automatically registers each lootbox as a usable item through the framework bridge. However, the item must still be **defined** in your inventory or framework's item list — the resource can only register the *use callback*, not create the item definition itself."},"1206":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-20","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#ox_core--ox_inventory-setup","content":"When using **ox\\_core**, usable items are handled through **ox\\_inventory** item definitions rather than the framework itself. For each lootbox case item, you need to add a `server.export` entry in your ox\\_inventory item definitions that points back to this resource."},"1207":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `ox_inventory/data/items.lua`:"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"The `server.export` value **must** follow the format `sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>`, where `<item_name>` matches the lootbox key defined in your `config.lua` or registered via exports. Without this, using the item will do nothing."},"1209":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"ox\\_inventory sees that the item has a `server.export` defined."},"1210":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-24","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"When a player uses the item, ox\\_inventory calls the matching export on `sleepless_lootbox`."},"1211":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-25","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The ox framework bridge registers these exports automatically when `config.registerUsableItems = true`."},"1212":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-26","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1213":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-27","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for ox\\_inventory:"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-28","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `server.export` — only the case items do."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-29","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1216":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-30","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"When using **QBCore** or **Qbox**, lootbox case items must be defined in your shared items table with `useable = true`. This allows the framework to register usable item callbacks."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-31","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `qb-core/shared/items.lua`:"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-32","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"The `useable = true` flag is **r